#!/bin/sh
HOST=$(hostname -s 2>/dev/null || echo fs-new)
cat << MOTD

freesounder player (${HOST})
------------------
This board is a locked-down appliance. The first-user wizard is disabled.
Use the FreeSounder app to set it up over Bluetooth or the local network.
The default hostname is fs-new; after you name the room in the app it
becomes fs-<room>. Local console login (tty2 and above) uses the fsadmin
account created at image build time. tty1 is a status screen, not a login.

  sudo freesounder-setup status
  sudo freesounder-setup doctor

SSH is off unless you enable developer mode from the app
(Settings → player → tap the version seven times). It turns itself off
again after a reboot.

MOTD
